  </div>

  <script>
    (function() {
      {% if product.handle == '5-courses-interior-exterior-design-ai' %}
      var ALL_REVIEWS = [{"id": 1, "name": "James Carter", "loc": "New York, NY", "ed": 1, "d": "Sep 21, 2026", "s": 5, "t": "The complete 2D-to-3D-to-AI pipeline for $49 is unheard of", "b": "Having AutoCAD, SketchUp, V-Ray, D5 Render, and AI in one unified curriculum completely transformed our firm. We draft the 2D permit sets in AutoCAD, model the architecture in SketchUp, do beauty shots in V-Ray, and present live variations in D5 Render AI. We closed a $14,000 residential project last week using this exact pipeline. Worth 50x the price.", "h": 46}, {"id": 2, "name": "Sophie Laurent", "loc": "London, UK", "ed": 1, "d": "Sep 20, 2026", "s": 5, "t": "D5 Render AI real-time walkthroughs doubled my close rate", "b": "I used to spend 3 days waiting for CPU test renders while clients grew impatient. The D5 Render AI course taught me how to navigate the model live during Zoom client meetings and tweak lighting on the fly. The clients gasped when they saw the real-time reflections and animated trees. Best $49 I have ever spent on design education.", "h": 39}, {"id": 3, "name": "Emma Rodriguez", "loc": "Los Angeles, CA", "ed": 1, "d": "Sep 19, 2026", "s": 5, "t": "Went from $250 flat drawings to $3,500 turnkey visualization packages", "b": "Before this bundle, I was struggling with fragmented YouTube tutorials. My SketchUp models were messy and V-Ray kept crashing. The instructors walk you through proper layer management, realistic PBR materials, and camera exposure. Plus, the 24/7 team support answered my GPU render settings within 20 minutes.", "h": 52}, {"id": 4, "name": "Daniel Chen", "loc": "Toronto, Canada", "ed": 0, "d": "Sep 18, 2026", "s": 5, "t": "Taught me what 3 years of university architecture school skipped", "b": "Architecture school taught abstract spatial theory but never showed how to actually build clean production blueprints in AutoCAD or photoreal V-Ray studio lighting. I completed all 5 courses over 3 weeks during summer break. I walked into interviews with an incredible portfolio and got hired at a top visualization studio.", "h": 41}, {"id": 5, "name": "Olivia Brooks", "loc": "Sydney, Australia", "ed": 1, "d": "Sep 17, 2026", "s": 5, "t": "The 10,000 textures & 2,000 3D models alone are worth $300", "b": "The curated asset library that comes with this bundle is insane. High-res seamless wood grains, fluted glass, boucl\u00e9 fabrics, and designer furniture ready to drag and drop into SketchUp. No more spending hours hunting sketchy free 3D warehouse models.", "h": 35}, {"id": 6, "name": "Marco Rossi", "loc": "Milan, Italy", "ed": 1, "d": "Sep 16, 2026", "s": 5, "t": "AI architectural ideation with Midjourney & Stable Diffusion is magic", "b": "The generative AI module is a game changer for client concept pitches. I can take a rough client iPad sketch or 2D floor plan, feed it into ControlNet/Midjourney, and generate 20 photorealistic aesthetic directions in 10 minutes. Clients are blown away before we even start the CAD drawings.", "h": 48}, {"id": 7, "name": "Sarah Klein", "loc": "Berlin, Germany", "ed": 0, "d": "Sep 15, 2026", "s": 5, "t": "AutoCAD blueprints module cleared up all site coordination issues", "b": "Contractors used to call me constantly about missing dimensions or unclear wall tags. The AutoCAD mastery course laid out professional layer standards, lineweights, and electrical layout symbols. Now our drawing packages look like they came from a 50-person architectural firm.", "h": 31}, {"id": 8, "name": "Ryan Murphy", "loc": "Dubai, UAE", "ed": 1, "d": "Sep 14, 2026", "s": 5, "t": "Photorealistic V-Ray sun & artificial lighting finally clicked", "b": "I could never get interior lighting right in V-Ray; it always looked washed out or artificially yellow. The module on IES light profiles, recessed LED downlights, and window bounce light made everything look like an Architectural Digest spread. Truly world-class instruction.", "h": 38}, {"id": 9, "name": "Chloe Patel", "loc": "Singapore", "ed": 1, "d": "Sep 13, 2026", "s": 5, "t": "Step-by-step from zero background to full renders", "b": "I had never touched 3D software before. Every lesson starts from the bare basics without skipping keystrokes or using confusing jargon. By Day 12, I had designed a custom Scandinavian kitchen in SketchUp and rendered it in both V-Ray and D5. Incredible confidence booster.", "h": 27}, {"id": 10, "name": "Alex Durand", "loc": "Barcelona, Spain", "ed": 0, "d": "Sep 12, 2026", "s": 5, "t": "The D5 Render AI video walkthrough workflow is unmatched", "b": "Rendering video animations used to take days of server farm time. With D5 Render AI, I render 60-second 4K fly-through videos on my RTX laptop in under 15 minutes. Clients share them on Instagram and it brings in a flood of inbound leads.", "h": 44}, {"id": 11, "name": "Nathan Reed", "loc": "Chicago, IL", "ed": 1, "d": "Sep 11, 2026", "s": 5, "t": "Perfect bridge between architectural drawings and client visualization", "b": "As a design-build contractor, bridging the gap between what clients see on paper and what we build is tough. Now we draft in AutoCAD, model in SketchUp, and render in D5 AI. Clients approve designs on the spot with zero misunderstandings.", "h": 33}, {"id": 12, "name": "Abigail Vance", "loc": "Auckland, NZ", "ed": 1, "d": "Sep 10, 2026", "s": 4, "t": "Incredible value, comprehensive curriculum", "b": "Five full courses with lifetime access and diplomas for $49 is unbeatable. The SketchUp custom millwork module and V-Ray displacement texture tutorials are worth the entire price alone. Highly recommended to any designer.", "h": 29}, {"id": 13, "name": "Carlos Mendoza", "loc": "Madrid, Spain", "ed": 1, "d": "Sep 9, 2026", "s": 5, "t": "24/7 team support helped fix my V-Ray displacement in minutes", "b": "I ran into a weird issue where my rug displacement wasn't calculating properly. I reached out to support and within minutes received a video reply pointing out the exact checkbox in V-Ray asset editor. That level of support for a $49 course is unmatched.", "h": 25}, {"id": 14, "name": "Hannah Wright", "loc": "Austin, TX", "ed": 0, "d": "Sep 8, 2026", "s": 5, "t": "Mastering the entire workflow gave me total career freedom", "b": "I quit my toxic corporate drafting job and went full freelance. I offer full packages now: 2D permit drawings in AutoCAD, 3D models in SketchUp, stills in V-Ray, and cinematic walkthroughs in D5 AI. I have more clients than I can handle.", "h": 37}, {"id": 15, "name": "Liam Scott", "loc": "Dublin, Ireland", "ed": 1, "d": "Sep 7, 2026", "s": 5, "t": "The AI module alone saved me 20 hours per concept", "b": "Being able to ideate architectural facades and modern interior palettes with prompt engineering in Midjourney before touching SketchUp is a superpower. You present 3 clear directions to clients in hour 1.", "h": 28}, {"id": 16, "name": "Zoe Takahashi", "loc": "Tokyo, Japan", "ed": 1, "d": "Sep 6, 2026", "s": 5, "t": "Clear, concise, no fluff, straight to professional execution", "b": "Most online courses spend 2 hours talking about theory before opening the software. Here you are drawing your first walls in AutoCAD and building 3D geometry in SketchUp in the very first module. Pure practical mastery.", "h": 32}, {"id": 17, "name": "Lucas Silva", "loc": "Sao Paulo, Brazil", "ed": 0, "d": "Sep 5, 2026", "s": 5, "t": "Best software training I have ever seen for architects", "b": "Covering the whole pipeline from 2D drafting all the way to generative AI ensures you don't get left behind by tech changes. If you are an architect or interior designer, this is a must-buy.", "h": 24}, {"id": 18, "name": "Priya Sharma", "loc": "Mumbai, India", "ed": 1, "d": "Sep 4, 2026", "s": 5, "t": "Certified digital diplomas helped me land overseas freelance gigs", "b": "The diplomas for AutoCAD, SketchUp, and V-Ray are recognized and look great on LinkedIn. Overseas clients specifically looked for designers proficient in both SketchUp and D5 Render AI. Paid back my $49 on day one.", "h": 40}];
      {% else %}
      var ALL_REVIEWS = [{"id":1,"name":"Sarah Martinez","loc":"Sydney, Australia","ed":1,"d":"Sep 13, 2026","s":4,"t":"The kitchen clearances alone saved us $4,000 on our remodel","b":"We were about to sign off on our cabinet contractor's layout when I checked Book 2. Our island was placed 34 inches from the range, way too tight. The diagrams clearly showed why 42 inches is the minimum working triangle clearance. We changed the plans before fabrication began. Worth 100x what I paid.","h":28},{"id":2,"name":"Michael White","loc":"New York, NY","ed":0,"d":"Sep 13, 2026","s":5,"t":"As an architecture student, this gave me what 3 years of college didn't","b":"Professors love teaching abstract architectural concepts and aesthetic philosophies, but when it comes to actual doorway clearances, stairs rise/run, or bathroom plumbing setbacks, nobody gives concrete numbers. These 6 books are packed with handmade diagrams that explain the real logic. I aced my thesis studio with them.","h":34},{"id":3,"name":"David Lewis","loc":"Melbourne, Australia","ed":0,"d":"Sep 12, 2026","s":5,"t":"The handmade diagrams make spatial planning click immediately","b":"Most design books are coffee table eye-candy with photos of $10M penthouses that offer zero actionable help. These books are completely different. Every page is hand-drawn with exact millimeter and inch dimensions, showing dos and don'ts side-by-side. You instantly see why a layout fails.","h":40},{"id":4,"name":"Emma Allen","loc":"Auckland, NZ","ed":1,"d":"Sep 11, 2026","s":5,"t":"Deluxe hardcopy quality is exceptional","b":"I ordered the complete hardcopy collection and was blown away by the printing. Thick archival paper, binding lays completely flat on my drafting desk, and the sketch reproductions are pin-sharp. Plus having the instant digital PDF on my iPad while on-site is the perfect combination.","h":31},{"id":5,"name":"James Wright","loc":"Amsterdam, Netherlands","ed":0,"d":"Sep 10, 2026","s":5,"t":"Transformed our aw